  "milestone_changes": [
    "Task 18 completes M9 with a strict uart_write/reset_and_run finalizer union on eligible serial tools, best-effort pre-cleanup ordering, owned process groups and markers, bounded identity-checked startup hygiene, and migration of production subprocess call sites to validated argv plus finite timeouts.",
    "Task 17 replaces abandoned timeout workers with request-tracked ManagedOperation lifecycles, one finite worker boundary per board, installed-SDK cancellation propagation, cooperative serial cancellation, non-interruptible flash completion, deterministic idempotent cleanup, explicit busy results, and cross-board concurrency.",
    "The Task 16 adversarial checkpoint pins exact outer and child board identities, bounded 1-64 child input, strict malformed-input rejection, disguised-recursion rejection, and preflight with zero authorization or budget consumption.",
    "Task 16 adds bounded same-board action_batch execution through each child's identical standard dispatch path, with structural whole-list preflight, nested-batch rejection, ordered stop-on-first-failure results, and no outer board lock.",
    "The action_batch outer timeout is derived from the sum of finite child direct-call timeouts so it cannot undercut an individual child's timeout while remaining bounded.",
    "The complete revised Layer-2 action surface is modular and board-scoped.",
    "The M7 audit closes the A-20 public surface: board_safety_setup and board_safety_refresh are registered, board-scoped, load-gated tools backed by authoritative server engines.",
    "Production freshness re-hashes only setup-selected pack and build artifact paths on every guarded write; build-only refresh derives replacement regions from those tracked artifacts.",
    "Legacy unified reset, core-register, raw memory, symbol-u32, and flash_firmware schemas are retired.",
    "Legacy unlock_recover is retired; target_unlock-plan and target_unlock provide the only automated destructive recovery surface.",
    "M8 binds a fresh one-time approval to the complete plan, live target and probe identities, connection, safety-map fingerprint, and map-derived erase disclosure.",
    "Full-session permission never authorizes mass erase, recovery is limited to typed vendor primitives, and successful recovery leaves the validation gate closed.",
    "The M8 checkpoint rejects incomplete erase evidence, invalidates prior authority on replacement disclosure, and proves cross-board and restart-default isolation plus authority-free reports.",
    "M7 enforces fail-closed RAM, peripheral, executable, flash partition, segment, entry/vector, exact-target, and erase-sector containment.",
    "Guarded reads require a board/connection validation stamp; write-capable actions additionally require an open gate and a current aggregate fingerprint on every call.",
    "M6 adds run-scoped setup disclosure, paired setup and repair actions, and bounded non-destructive validation.",
    "M6 component hashes pin preflight, research, target and pack resolution, workflow state, cache, reports, server composition, and the shared Stage 0/BoardValidator implementation path.",
    "Validation steps 8 and 9 now verify map consistency and stamp only the successful board/connection; gate authority remains run-scoped and is never persisted.",
    "Safety refresh may update an existing active validation stamp after a successful scoped rebuild but cannot create or reopen a closed gate.",
    "M6 hardware acceptance adds isolated artifact roots, stable plan-bound setup inventory, official target mapping with exact part-consistency checks, the validation code in MCP payloads, and explicit pyOCD attach mode for non-resetting validation."
  ],
